
1. int length() : Returns the number of characters in the String.
  String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.length()); // 13

2 .charAt(int i)  : This method returns the character at ith index.

3 .String substring(int i)  :This method return the substring from the ith index character to end.
   String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.substring(7)); // World

4 .  String substring(int i, int j) : This method returns the substring from i to j-1 index.
     String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.substring(7, 12)); // World

5. String concat( String str)
     String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.concat("!!!"));

6.int indexOf(String s) : This method returns the index within the string of the first occurrence of the specified string.
If the specified string s is not found in the input string, the method returns -1 by default.
   String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.indexOf("World"));// 10

7.int indexOf(String s, int i) : This method returns the index within the string of the first occurrence of the specified string,
starting at the specified index
  String str = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(str.indexOf("l", 4)); //10

8.int lastIndexOf(String s) : This method returns the index within the string of the last occurrence of the specified string.
 If the specified string s is not found in the input string, the method returns -1 by default.
    String s = "Hello, World!";
         System.out.println(s.lastIndexOf("l"));//10

 9.boolean equals(Object otherObj) : This method compares this string to the specified object.
        String s = "Hello, World!";
         System.out.println(s.equals("Hello, World!")); //true

 10.int compareTo(String anotherString) :This method compares two string lexicographically
  String s = "Hello, World!";
    System.out.println(s.compareTo("Hello, Java!")); //13

 11.boolean equalsIgnoreCase(String anotherString) : This method checks if two strings are equal,
 without considering letter case.
  String s = "Hello, World!";
         System.out.println(s.compareToIgnoreCase("hello, java!"));//13

 12.String trim()
 This method returns the copy of the String, by removing whitespaces at both ends.
  It does not modify the whitespace characters present between the text.

 13.String replace(char oldChar, char newChar) : This method returns a new string where all
  instances of oldChar are replaced by newChar.
    String s = "Hello, World!";
          System.out.println(s.replace('l', 'x'));// Hexxo, Worxd!

 14. boolean contains(CharSequence sequence) : This method returns true if string contains the given string.
    String s = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(s.contains("World")); // true

 15.boolean startsWith(String prefix) : This method returns true if string starts with this prefix.
         String s = "Hello, World!";
         System.out.println(s.startsWith("Hello"));